    <h2>6 · Games &amp; activities</h2>
    <p>A bank of ways to use the tool, grouped by developmental stage. Pick the group that matches the learner and move up or down as needed.</p>

    <h3>A. Sense &amp; respond (Levels A–B)</h3>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Make it sing</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Support the child (hand‑over‑hand if needed) to press a key; react with delight; wait; invite another press.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> attention, cause‑and‑effect, intentional action.</div><div class="tag">Music: Exploring · English: S&amp;L. Easier: one bright key. Harder: offer two keys to choose.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Copy me (call &amp; response)</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> You press a key, then invite the child to press one. Build a simple back‑and‑forth.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> turn‑taking, imitation, joint attention.</div><div class="tag">Music: Exploring · English: S&amp;L. Harder: copy a two‑key pattern.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Colour hunt</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Name or show a colour (use the chart); help the child find and press that key.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> colour matching, scanning, targeting.</div><div class="tag">Music: Exploring · English: S&amp;L. Harder: find the colour then name the note.</div></div>
    </div>

    <h3>B. Letters &amp; sounds (Levels C–D / Foundation)</h3>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Find the letter</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Say a letter name or its sound (“find /m/”). The child locates and presses that key.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> letter recognition, letter–sound knowledge.</div><div class="tag">English: Phonics · Music: Exploring. Harder: find three letters in a row.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">My name song</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Help the child type their own name and press ▶ to hear it as a tune.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> recognising letters in own name, left‑to‑right order.</div><div class="tag">English: Writing · Music: Creating. Easier: pre‑type the name; they press play.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">First sound</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Show a picture; the child presses the key for its beginning sound (cat → C).</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> initial phoneme awareness, letter–sound links.</div><div class="tag">English: Phonics · Music: Exploring. Harder: first and last sound.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Rainbow letters</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Match a letter on the printed chart to the same key on screen and play it.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> letter matching, print‑to‑screen transfer.</div><div class="tag">English: Language · Music: Exploring. Harder: match a short set to spell a word.</div></div>
    </div>

    <h3>C. Words &amp; sentences (Foundation / Level 1)</h3>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Word of the day</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Choose a simple word (cat, sun, mum); sound it out, build it key by key, then play it.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> blending sounds, building CVC words.</div><div class="tag">English: Phonics/Literacy · Music: Creating. Easier: a two‑letter word.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Silly sentence</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Build a short, fun sentence (“we can hop”). Press ▶ to hear its melody.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> sentence concept, word order, word spaces.</div><div class="tag">English: Literacy · Music: Creating. Harder: add a describing word.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Where do the rests go?</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Type a sentence and watch spaces become one‑beat rests; clap the words, pausing on rests.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> word boundaries, beat and rest.</div><div class="tag">English: Writing · Music: Exploring/Creating. Harder: count the rests.</div></div>
    </div>

    <h3>D. Copy &amp; type — Follow‑along (Foundation – Level 2)</h3>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Copy the sentence</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> In Follow‑along mode, the child copies the highlighted target letter by letter; finishing earns a ⭐.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> accuracy, one‑to‑one matching, keyboarding.</div><div class="tag">English: Writing · Music: Developing Practices. Harder: turn Notes off, longer sentence.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Grown‑up sets the goal</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Use the ⚙️ For grown‑ups button to set a target matching this week's learning (a name, a word, a topic sentence).</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> targeted vocabulary/sentence practice.</div><div class="tag">English: Writing/Literacy · Music: Developing Practices.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Two‑star challenge</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Set a small goal — finish two sentences to earn two stars; track stars across the session.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> goal‑setting, self‑regulation, resilience.</div><div class="tag">English: Writing · Personal &amp; Social Capability.</div></div>
    </div>

    <h3>E. Rhythm &amp; composing (Levels 1–2)</h3>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Long and short</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Clap a short rhythm; then tap tiles to set matching note lengths (½, 1, 2, 4) and play it back.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> beat vs rhythm, note values.</div><div class="tag">Music: Creating · English: patterning. Harder: match a four‑note pattern.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Name that value</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Point to a tile; the child names its length — quaver, crotchet, minim or semibreve.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> music vocabulary, symbol–value matching.</div><div class="tag">Music: Developing Practices/Creating. Harder: order shortest to longest.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Compose a four‑beat bar</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Make the notes in one dashed bar add to four beats (e.g. two minims). Play and check.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> counting beats, composing in 4/4.</div><div class="tag">Music: Creating · Numeracy. Harder: two bars, different rhythms.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Fast and slow</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> Play the same sentence at Slow, then Fast. Talk about how the feeling changes.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> tempo, expression, musical choices.</div><div class="tag">Music: Exploring · English: S&amp;L. Harder: match a tempo to a mood word.</div></div>
    </div>

    <h3>F. Perform &amp; respond (Levels 1–2)</h3>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">Mini concert</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> The child performs their finished sentence‑tune to a partner or the class, pressing ▶ and introducing it.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> performing, confidence, oral language.</div><div class="tag">Music: Presenting · English: S&amp;L. Easier: perform to one adult.</div></div>
      <div class="cardx"><div class="nm">I like… I would change…</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Play:</span> After a peer's tune, each child says one thing they liked and one gentle idea to try.</div><div class="row"><span class="k">Builds:</span> listening, expressing preferences with reasons.</div><div class="tag">Music: Responding · English: S&amp;L. Harder: give a reason.</div></div>
    </div>

    <!-- 7 -->
    <h2>7 · Differentiation &amp; access (Universal Design for Learning)</h2>
    <h3>Ways in (engagement)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Follow the child's interest — start with their name, a favourite word, or a topic they love.</li>
      <li>Use the ⭐ stars and short goals to motivate; keep sessions short and successful.</li>
      <li>Because every tune stays in key, mistakes still sound good — this protects confidence.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Ways to show it (representation)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Turn Notes on to reveal note names; turn them off as skills grow.</li>
      <li>Pair the screen with the printed colour chart so learning transfers between print and device.</li>
      <li>Colour, letter, sound and note length give four ways to recognise the same key.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Ways to respond (action &amp; expression)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Tap on a tablet or type on a keyboard; use one finger, a pointer, or hand‑over‑hand support.</li>
      <li>Slow the tempo for learners who need more time between beats.</li>
      <li>Work one letter at a time in Follow‑along mode; the target waits patiently.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Sensory &amp; wellbeing</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>If a learner is sensitive to movement, turn on the device's “reduce motion” setting — the app calms its animations automatically.</li>
      <li>Manage volume, offer headphones, and watch for over‑stimulation; the predictable, in‑key sound is designed to be calming.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- 8 -->
    <h2>8 · Observing &amp; recording learning</h2>
    <p>Children may show learning in different ways depending on their communication, physical access and needs. Watch for these signs, which align with the achievement‑standard language of the relevant levels.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Attends to, and acts to repeat, a sound (Levels A–B).</li>
      <li>Presses a named letter and links it to a sound (Levels C–D).</li>
      <li>Builds and plays a short word or simple sentence (Level D – Foundation).</li>
      <li>Copies a modelled sentence accurately in Follow‑along mode (Foundation – Level 1).</li>
      <li>Sets note lengths and keeps a four‑beat bar (Levels 1–2).</li>
      <li>Performs a tune and says what they like or would change (Levels 1–2).</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted small">A printable observation record is included in the Word and PDF versions of this guide (Downloads above).</p>

